# round 125 (w142): which half of the betaxanthin store carries round 117's gain. The store is growth vector | production vector (suffix __btx) | btx_total_demand. bxgrowth keeps the growth block and the total-demand column (4,178 of 8,355); bxprod keeps the production block (4,177). Everything else as w134_bxstore, paired by seed against it and against w134_bxctx. Round 119 measured that two summary columns and a decayed, slowed affine both lose the gain, so the question is which fine structure the affine reads.
